# Deny-all then allowlist. `code/` accumulates .snakemake/, conda trees and large
# intermediates, so the safe default is "ignored" and tracked paths are named explicitly.
#
# *** A NEW FILE TYPE OR DIRECTORY HERE IS SILENTLY NOT COMMITTED UNTIL YOU ADD A LINE. ***
# `git status` will not mention it. `git check-ignore -v <path>` names the rule that caught it.
*
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.editorconfig
!README.md
!Snakefile
!config
!config/*
!schemas
!schemas/*
!rules
!rules/*
!envs
!envs/*
!scripts
!scripts/*
!scripts/common
!scripts/common/*
scripts/.snakemake*
!jobs
!jobs/*
!module_workflows
!module_workflows/*
!snakemake_profiles
!snakemake_profiles/**
!scratch
!scratch/.gitkeep
!logs
!logs/.gitkeep
*.swp
.ipynb_checkpoints/
